# MOSAIC — Project Context for Claude Code

## What This Project Is

MOSAIC (Modular Orchestrated Sub-Agent Architecture for Imitation-based Control) is a hierarchical multi-agent robotics system built as a first research paper. The task is shape sorting — a robot arm must find a block, pick it up, navigate to the correct slot based on its shape, and insert it. There are 4 shapes: circle, square, triangle, star.

The core research contribution is the orchestrator and modular policy architecture. Instead of one end-to-end ACT policy trained on the full task, MOSAIC uses three specialized ACT policies sequenced by a GPT-4o orchestrator that can detect failures and replan. This is compared against a single end-to-end ACT baseline in evaluation.

---

## Hardware

- **Robot arm:** SO101 manipulator
- **Motors:** Feetech STS3215 servo motors — servo position is readable and used as a force proxy since there is no F/T sensor
- **Cameras:** Overhead camera (workspace view) + gripper camera (close-up end effector view)
- **No force/torque sensor** — all contact detection uses servo position thresholds

