## Camera and Frame Processing

**Raw frames only.** Both cameras output raw frames with no preprocessing. CLAHE was tested and made results worse on this hardware so it was removed. The raw frame from the overhead camera is used for both GPT-4V shape classification and as ACT policy input. The raw frame from the gripper camera is used as ACT policy input only.

**Critical rule:** Training frames and inference frames must be identical. Whatever the camera outputs during demo recording is what the ACT policy sees at inference time. No preprocessing is applied at either stage.

**Two uses of the overhead frame — never mixed:**
- Raw frame → GPT-4V for shape classification (orchestrator layer)
- Raw frame → ACT policy observation (agent layer)

Both branches read from the same capture. The frame is never modified before going to ACT.

