## Data Collection Protocol

Episodes are recorded as **full end-to-end demonstrations** — home position → grasp → navigate → insert — in one continuous recording. Keyframe annotations mark the two transition points. A post-processing script then splits each full episode into three sub-episodes, one per policy.

**Why full episodes instead of separate phase demos:**
- More natural to teleoperate — no stopping and resetting between phases
- Start/end states of each sub-policy are guaranteed to be consistent with each other
- One teleoperation session yields three training examples
- Transition states (e.g. carry height after grasp) are learned from real continuations, not artificial resets

### Recording a Demo

1. Arm starts at home position, block placed somewhere in workspace
2. Start recording: `bash scripts/record_session_a.sh` (or equivalent)
3. Teleoperate the full task:
   - Pick up the block from anywhere in the workspace
   - Lift it to carry height
   - **Press `k`** → marks Keyframe 1 (grasp complete)
   - Navigate to the correct slot above it
   - **Press `k`** → marks Keyframe 2 (navigate complete)
   - Insert the block into the slot
   - End the episode (spacebar or configured stop key)
4. Repeat for all 4 shapes, varying block position each time

### Keyframe Annotation

Two keyframes are pressed per episode:

| Keyframe | When to press | Marks |
|---|---|---|
| KF1 | Block is in gripper, arm lifted to carry height | End of grasp phase |
| KF2 | Arm is positioned directly above the correct slot | End of navigate phase |

Keyframe timestamps are stored as metadata on the episode. The split script uses them as slice boundaries.

### Dataset Split

After recording, run the split script to generate three training datasets from one:

```
full episode [frame 0 → frame N]
     │
     ├── [0  → KF1]  → datasets/grasp/
     ├── [KF1→ KF2]  → datasets/navigate_<shape>/
     └── [KF2→ N  ]  → datasets/insert/
```

Script: `scripts/split_episodes.py` (reads keyframe metadata, writes three LeRobotDataset splits)

### Demo Targets

- **50 full episodes per shape** → 50 grasp demos + 50 navigate demos per shape + 50 insert demos
- **200 full episodes total** (50 × 4 shapes)
- Vary block position across the full workspace on every episode
- Include episodes with slight misalignment before insert — ACT will learn the search/wiggle correction

