## The Three ACT Policies

All policies are trained using LeRobot's ACT implementation on the SO101. Observations for all policies include overhead camera frame, gripper camera frame, and joint positions. All training data comes from splitting full end-to-end episodes at keyframe boundaries (see Data Collection Protocol above).

### Policy 1 — Grasp Policy
- **Trained on:** Frames 0 → KF1 from all 200 full episodes (all shapes)
- **Start state:** Arm at home position, block somewhere in workspace
- **End state:** Block held in gripper, arm lifted to carry height
- **Varies across demos:** Block position across full workspace, all 4 shapes
- **Checkpoint:** `checkpoints/grasp/`

### Policy 2 — Navigate Policies (4 total, one per shape)
- **Trained on:** Frames KF1 → KF2 from the 50 episodes for that shape
- **Start state:** Arm at carry height holding block
- **End state:** Arm positioned directly above the correct slot, ready to insert
- **Why separate per shape:** Each shape has a different target slot position. Training separate policies avoids shape conditioning complexity and keeps each policy simple and focused.
- **Checkpoints:** `checkpoints/navigate_circle/`, `checkpoints/navigate_square/`, `checkpoints/navigate_triangle/`, `checkpoints/navigate_star/`

### Policy 3 — Insert Policy
- **Trained on:** Frames KF2 → end from all 200 full episodes (all shapes)
- **Start state:** Arm above slot holding block
- **End state:** Block fully inserted, gripper released
- **Note:** Because insert demos come from all 4 shapes, the policy sees varied slot approach angles — this improves robustness naturally.
- **Checkpoint:** `checkpoints/insert/`

