## Paper Metrics

Run 20 trials per shape for both MOSAIC and the single ACT baseline (80 trials each, 160 total).

| Metric | Description |
|---|---|
| Overall task success rate | % trials where block correctly inserted |
| Per-shape success rate | Breakdown by circle/square/triangle/star |
| Recovery rate | % of failure cases where replanning led to success |
| Average retries per trial | How often replanning was needed |
| Average time to completion | Total ms including retries |

The key comparison is recovery rate — the baseline single ACT policy gets zero recoveries because it has no replanning. MOSAIC recovers from mid-task failures. This is the central claim of the paper.

