## Key Implementation Rules

1. **Never preprocess frames before ACT.** Raw frames only. Training and inference must match exactly.
2. **Never draw overlays on frames going to ACT.** Debug visualizations go on copies only.
3. **Capture observation once per timestep.** Do not open the camera twice. One `robot.capture_observation()` call, reuse the dict everywhere.
4. **Log everything from day one.** Every trial, every phase, every retry. This data is your paper results.
5. **Calibrate servo thresholds on your hardware before evaluation.** The numbers in this doc are starting points not ground truth.
6. **Test each agent in isolation before wiring the orchestrator.** Grasp alone, navigate alone, insert alone, then full pipeline.
7. **Press keyframes deliberately, not reactively.** KF1 should be pressed when the arm is stable at carry height — not mid-motion. A sloppy keyframe creates a bad sub-episode boundary for both adjacent policies.
8. **Run split_episodes.py before training.** Never train directly on full episodes. The split script is the source of truth for all three datasets.

